 ## Initialisation and Privacy
 
-- `init` creates a bounded, deterministic, non-semantic baseline from package metadata, safe filesystem enumeration, language-count extensions, and workflow filenames.
-- Every baseline directory source reads at most 513 raw entries before filtering and is bound to a stable real-directory generation. Recursive traversal schedules at most 10,000 directories, binds each child capture to its enumerated parent, and accepts all baseline source passes only while the repository-root generation remains stable. The package pass always opens the literal root `package.json`; exact casing wins when case-distinct aliases coexist, while an enumerated alias supplies attribution only when that literal open succeeds on a case-insensitive filesystem. Validated top-level presence distinguishes a package or `.github` source that disappears before its preliminary metadata check from ordinary absence. Overflow, unreadable directories, workflow enumeration failures, and invalid, oversized, or stably unreadable package metadata omit the affected facts and set `scanTruncated` with bounded, ordinal-sorted reason codes in the repository overview. Package replacement or other source change discards the complete attempt instead.
+- `init` creates a bounded, deterministic, non-semantic baseline from verified root package metadata, a bounded root directory snapshot, and workflow filenames. It does not traverse source directories or generate language counts or regular-file totals; agents may discover these separately.
+- Every baseline directory source reads at most 513 raw entries before filtering and is bound to a stable real-directory generation. Only the root and `.github/workflows` are enumerated; workflow ancestry and all retained baseline sources must share a stable repository-root generation. The package pass always opens the literal root `package.json`; exact casing wins when case-distinct aliases coexist, while an enumerated alias supplies attribution only when that literal open succeeds on a case-insensitive filesystem. Validated top-level presence distinguishes a package or `.github` source that disappears before its preliminary metadata check from ordinary absence. Overflow, unreadable directories, workflow enumeration failures, and invalid, oversized, or stably unreadable package metadata omit the affected facts and set `scanTruncated` with bounded, ordinal-sorted reason codes in the repository overview. Package replacement or other source change discards the complete attempt instead.
 - Baseline payload assembly retains compact root, directory, package-content, absence, and expected-failure evidence and revalidates all of it together before acceptance. A changed attempt is discarded in full and retried within one baseline-owned ledger of at most three complete attempts and one non-resetting 60-second deadline, checked before a retry. Stable expected failures retain their deterministic truncation reasons; persistent churn returns concise path-free `REPOSITORY_CHANGED`.
-- The complete baseline reason vocabulary is `directory-entry-limit`, `directory-limit`, `max-depth`, `package-metadata-error`, `regular-file-limit`, `top-level-entry-limit`, `unreadable-directory`, `workflow-entry-limit`, and `workflow-enumeration-error`.
+- The complete baseline reason vocabulary is `package-metadata-error`, `top-level-entry-limit`, `unreadable-directory`, `workflow-entry-limit`, and `workflow-enumeration-error`.
+- The generated overview contains `recognisedTopLevelFiles`, `topLevelDirectories`, `sources`, `summary`, `scanTruncated`, and `scanTruncationReasons`. Tooling and command records retain their existing package, workspace, manager, script-argv, and workflow fields. The existing JSON search projection indexes these retained facts; init adds no separate source inventory or search text.
+- Ordinary `init` preserves existing generated heads. Explicit `init --refresh-baseline` appends a replacement for each changed generated subject and supersedes all its prior active generated heads; unchanged subjects keep their current records. Historical payloads, including language counts and file totals, remain valid, byte-for-byte unchanged, and searchable with superseded records included. A repeated refresh over unchanged shallow sources appends nothing.
 - `init` may read root `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` byte-for-byte only to manage the Encephalon block while preserving unrelated bytes.
 - Unrelated instruction text, source bodies, README content, environment files, registry configuration, Git history, Git remotes, and CI workflow contents must not enter generated records, cache search text, stdout, or structured error details.
 - The managed instruction block points agents to `./node_modules/encephalon/skills/encephalon/SKILL.md` and remains exactly reversible where Encephalon created or updated it.
